   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preparation of Kigali HFC implementation plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MALAWI - Preparation of Kigali HFC implementation plan.  Malawi has ratified the Montreal Protocol and its Kigali amendments, which regulate their production and consumption of ODS and HFCs. At the 93rd ExCom Meeting, Stage I of the HFC phase-down plan, which is also known as the Kigali Implementation Plan (KIP),  was approved with a grant of USD 170,000. The objective of the KIP Stage I is to progressively phase-down its use of HFCs by 10% before 2029.  HFC baseline is 428,435 CO2 eq., which is calculated as the average consumption level over 2020, 2021 and 2022, plus 65% of their HCFC baseline consumption. Malawi neither produces nor exports HFCs. Pure refrigerant HFC-134a and mixtures R-410A, R-404A, R-507A, R-407A and R-407C are the only imported HFCs and are consumed solely for servicing RAC or MAC equipment.  UNEP is the lead agency and UNIDO is the cooperating agency for the execution of the KIP. The National Ozone Unit (NOU) in the Environmental Affairs Department, Malawi is national counterpart for the implement of KIP.</narrative>
  </description>
